    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161">

                <pb facs="0260" n="158" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg158"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/1972</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Liberian Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Barclay</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the American Chargé</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Macy</hi>)<anchor n="35" xml:id="d161-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-08-20"><hi rendition="#italic">August 20,
                        1927</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">870/D</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Chargé d’Affaires</hi>: I have the honour to
                    acknowledge receipt of your communication dated July 30, 1927,<anchor n="36"
                        xml:id="d161-f2"/> informing the Government <pb facs="0261" n="159"
                        xml:id="pg159"/> of Liberia that, the President and the Secretary of State
                    of the United States, having been advised that suitable provision has been made
                    for the extinguishment of the 1912 loan, take pleasure in assuming the functions
                    assigned to them under the terms of the Loan Agreement of September 1, 1926.</p>
                <p>Replying to the penultimate paragraph of your communication,<anchor n="37"
                        xml:id="d161-f3"/> I have the honour to say that the President’s designation
                    of Mr. Sidney de la Rue to the President of Liberia for appointment as Financial
                    Adviser to the Republic of Liberia, is agreeable and acceptable to the Liberian
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin Barclay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d161-f1" n="35" type="source" xml:id="d161-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department by the Chargé in Liberia in his despatch No.
                    511, Sept. 13; received Nov. 4.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d161-f2" n="36" xml:id="d161-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 23, July 29, to the Chargé in Liberia, <ref target="#pg156">p.
                        156</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d161-f3" n="37" xml:id="d161-f3-content">
                <p>Second paragraph of note as transmitted in Department’s telegram No. 23, July
                    29.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
